  (text "Y" (at 166.37 159.4 0)
    (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top))
    (uuid 75edfbfd-7b01-471c-9081-00d2cd22be17)
  )
  (text "Input subsystem (pilink-7el.6, amended by pilink-cmn then pilink-3rm):\n4 discrete tact buttons (A/B/X/Y) + 1 rotary encoder -- 5 inputs total,\ndown from the original 8-switch d-pad+buttons layout. See\n.planning/decisions/2026-11-14-dpad-instead-of-joystick.md (original\nd-pad ADR), .planning/decisions/2026-11-15-rotary-encoder-for-volume.md\n(replaced LEFT/RIGHT with the encoder), and\n.planning/decisions/2026-11-15-rotary-encoder-replaces-full-dpad.md\n(removed UP/DOWN too, freeing GPIO20/21 back into\nrp2350b_memory.kicad_sch's generic pool). The encoder is now the sole\ndirectional control, serving double duty by firmware context (volume or\nmenu up/down on rotation, select/mute on press) -- firmware's job\n(../pico-link, not this repo), not this hardware's. There is no\ndedicated PRESS/select net on this sheet -- firmware remaps select/OK\nonto one of A/B/X/Y itself." (at 220 15 0)
    (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top))
    (uuid 06d6a717-f00b-43da-b3c4-49d4780d0282)
  )
  (text "Pull resistor convention: each switch gets its own external 10k pull-up\n(R305-R308) from +3V3 to the GPIO node; the switch itself\n(SW305-SW308) pulls that node to GND when pressed --\nactive-low, pressed = logic 0. The rotary encoder (SW303) follows the same\nconvention for all 3 of its signals: quadrature channels A and B are each\nexternally pulled up to +3V3 (R304, R303) and pulled toward GND through\nthe encoder's internal mechanical contact against its common pin C (wired\ndirectly to GND); the integrated push-switch (pins S1/S2) is wired the\nsame way -- S2 pulled up to +3V3 through R309, S1 wired directly to GND\n(S1/S2 are an unpolarized SPST contact pair per the datasheet, so which\nterminal is pulled up is an arbitrary but documented choice, not a\nfunctional constraint). Alps' EC11E18244AU datasheet (see part-citation\nnote below) rates the encoder's contacts at 10mA max / 1mA min and\nspecifies no internal pull resistors, so external pull-ups are required\nexactly as for the discrete switches, but sized 3.3k (10k only gives\n~0.33mA) -- same reasoning as this sheet's original pull-up note: ordinary\nGPIOs have no guaranteed default pull state, so an explicit external\npull-up keeps each input well-defined independent of firmware GPIO init\norder. This differs from rp2350b_memory.kicad_sch's BOOTSEL/reset switches\n(SW101/SW102), which rely on the boot-ROM's own QSPI_SS handling and RUN's\ninternal pull-up respectively and fit no external pull-up -- those are\nspecial-function pins with documented default behavior." (at 220 54 0)
    (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top))
    (uuid 6405952e-260e-4bf6-8c01-8d8442176dae)
  )
  (text "GPIO net assignment: GPIO24-27 unchanged (A=24, B=25, X=26, Y=27),\npicked from the generic bidirectional GPIO pool rp2350b_memory.kicad_sch\nexposes as global labels for every RP2350B GPIO not already committed to\nthat sheet's own circuitry (GPIO47/PSRAM_CS is the only pin withheld\nfrom that pool). The first 2026-11-15 amendment (pilink-cmn) reused the\ntwo GPIOs freed by removing LEFT/RIGHT (GPIO22, GPIO23) for the rotary\nencoder's quadrature channels A and B, and claimed one additional GPIO\n(GPIO28, the next free pin in the pool) for the encoder's push-switch --\nconfirmed free by grepping all 4 populated sheets (power,\nrp2350b_memory, esp32_bt, input) for every GPIO/ESP32_*/ global label\nbefore finalizing: no sibling sheet claims GPIO22, GPIO23, or GPIO28.\nThe second 2026-11-15 amendment (pilink-3rm) removed UP/DOWN entirely,\nfreeing GPIO20/21 back into that pool, same cross-sheet convention as\nesp32_bt.kicad_sch's ESP32_* global labels: sibling child sheets join\nsame-named nets project-wide via a global label, no hierarchical sheet\npins or root-sheet wiring needed. Each switch/signal also carries its\nfirmware-facing logical name (A/B/X/Y, VOL_A/VOL_B/VOL_SW for the\nencoder) as a plain text caption -- deliberately NOT a second schematic\nlabel on the same net: a global label and a local label both landing on\none net connect fine electrically, but ERC reports it as\nmultiple_net_names (the global label wins in the netlist either way), so\nthe logical name is documentation-only graphical text here instead, with\nno electrical meaning and nothing for ERC to flag." (at 220 109 0)
    (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top))
    (uuid 3c0ca8f7-c187-466d-9449-00281f05387b)
  )
  (text "Reference designators use this project's per-sheet numbering block\n300-399 (power.kicad_sch: 1-99, rp2350b_memory.kicad_sch: 100-199,\nesp32_bt.kicad_sch: 200-299) so no two sibling sheets' components can\nmerge into the same netlist part. The first 2026-11-15 amendment\n(pilink-cmn) retired SW304 (old RIGHT -- gap, not reused) and\nrepurposed SW303 for the rotary encoder, reusing R303/R304 as its two\nquadrature pull-ups and adding R309 as the push-switch's pull-up;\n#PWR305/#PWR307 (freed +3V3) and #PWR306/#PWR308 (freed GND) reuse for\nthe encoder, plus new #PWR317 (+3V3). The second 2026-11-15 amendment\n(pilink-3rm) retired SW301/SW302, R301/R302, and #PWR301-#PWR304 the\nsame way -- gaps, not reused. A/B/X/Y keep their original SW305-SW308,\nR305-R308, and #PWR309-#PWR316 unchanged. No PWR_FLAG on this sheet,\nmatching rp2350b_memory.kicad_sch's and esp32_bt.kicad_sch's own\nreasoning -- this sheet doesn't generate +3V3/GND, power.kicad_sch\ndoes, so a standalone ERC run on this sheet alone is expected to report\npower_pin_not_driven for both rails; the root sheet (which flattens the\nwhole hierarchy and sees the regulator) is the real check. See\nhardware/README.md for both ERC runs and the project-wide netlist\ncollision check. FLAG for firmware integration (out of scope here):\nfirmware's current PL_INPUT_PIN_* pin NUMBERS\n(2/18/16/20/15/17/19/21, the old Waveshare board's GPIO map) still\nneed remapping, and PL_INPUT_PIN_LEFT/RIGHT/UP/DOWN all go away\nentirely for a new quadrature-decode + push-button path for the\nencoder, now the device's sole directional control -- tracked as\nfollow-up bead pilink-otf (pin remap) plus not-yet-filed encoder\nfirmware work flagged in both 2026-11-15 rotary-encoder ADRs." (at 220 164 0)
    (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top))
    (uuid 9846e71a-aed5-4181-b0cc-b62ef7d1a9ec)
  )
  (text "Rotary encoder part choice (pilink-cmn): Alps Alpine EC11E18244AU --\nJLCPCB/LCSC C202365, Extended-library part (not Basic -- standard\nextended-part handling fee, not a sourcing-availability risk). Verified\nagainst Alps' own published datasheet, retrieved via LCSC's direct PDF\n(datasheet.lcsc.com/datasheet/pdf/00ace576d31da40a390056171db2037f.pdf --\nlcsc.com/datasheet/C202365.pdf resolves to an HTML viewer, not the PDF, so\nthe symbol's Datasheet field and this citation use the direct link):\nVertical structure, flat actuator, 20mm actuator length, 36 detents / 18\npulses, two-phase incremental output (terminals A, B, common C),\nintegrated push-on switch (SPST, 0.5mm travel, 0.1A/5V DC rating,\nterminals labeled D/E on the datasheet -- mapped onto this sheet's S1/S2\npins), 10mA/5V DC max rating overall, no internal pull resistors (hence\nthe external pull-ups on all 3 signals, see the pull-resistor-convention\nnote above). Symbol: stock KiCad library Device:RotaryEncoder_Switch (5\npins: A, B, C, S1, S2 -- exact match for this part's A/B/C/D/E pinout).\nFootprint: stock KiCad library\nRotary_Encoder:RotaryEncoder_Alps_EC11E-Switch_Vertical_H20mm --\npurpose-built for an Alps EC11E + integrated switch + vertical mount +\n20mm shaft, i.e. this specific part family/variant, not a generic\nstand-in. Live stock re-checked 2026-11-15 against LCSC's own C202365\nproduct page: approximately 2,482 units in stock -- a live-changing figure\n(other snapshots the same day ranged roughly 2,500-4,300 depending on\ncache/mirror), so treat this as a point-in-time reading, not\nguaranteed-current." (at 220 233 0)
    (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top))
    (uuid 9179a531-c9a3-4f5d-a7fc-337028bcbb9e)
  )
)
